Vercel XHTTP relay (VercelRelay.kt, VercelRelayController.kt, assets/vercel/*)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The idea of relaying Xray XHTTP traffic through a Vercel function comes from the public
projects B3hnamR/XHTTPRelayECO, alirezaparvas/vercel-xhttp-relay, SNI-XHTTP and
Maahdima/Vercel-XHTTP (guides and YouTube walkthroughs). Those repositories publish no licence,
so no code was copied: the relay scripts, the deployment client and the UI were written
independently for Cat Client (GPL-3.0).

Cat Panel on Vercel (VercelPanel.kt, assets/vercel/panel-adapter.mjs)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The approach of serving VLESS-over-WebSocket from a Vercel Node function
(`http.createServer` + the `ws` package, a `cloudflare:sockets`-style connect()
shim on top of `node:net`) follows ludas114343/vercel-vless-proxy
(https://github.com/ludas114343/vercel-vless-proxy), MIT License,
Copyright (c) ludas114343. The adapter in Cat Client was written independently
around the existing Cat Panel worker; the MIT notice above is kept as attribution.

Cat SSTP (SstpClient.kt)
------------------------
The SSTP client follows the published specifications ([MS-SSTP], RFC 1661, 1332,
1334, 1994, 2759 and 3079). The MD4 routine and the HLAK / Compound-MAC
derivation of the SSTP crypto binding were written after Open SSTP Client by
KOBAYASHI Ittoku (https://github.com/kittoku/Open-SSTP-Client), MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2019 KOBAYASHI Ittoku. Permission is hereby granted, free of
charge, to any person obtaining a copy of that software, to deal in it without
restriction, subject to including the copyright notice and this permission
notice; the software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind.
The public server list is read at run time from sstp.wireconf.workers.dev
(VPN Gate servers, University of Tsukuba volunteer project); no data is bundled.
